## Audit already done

A seven-pass pre-launch audit found and fixed 7 blockers, 16 serious and 7 minor issues. `docs/PRE_LAUNCH.md` holds the record and the go-live checklist. The worst finding: the app had two canonical phone formats and didn't know it, so one person could become two un-matchable records — dangerous for a DNC-sensitive business. A later pass found `sessions:get` was returning any session to any authenticated caller by sequential id, with the export built on that same read.

## Decisions already made — please don't reverse these without asking

- Re-pooling leads **grants** extra attempts, never resets `attempts_count` — that count is a compliance record of how many times a real person was telephoned.
- Campaign tiles count every source; only the funnel is scoped to dialer-originated calls.
- Rates are never computed from samples too small to mean anything; users are compared against the team median, never ranked best/worst.
- Nothing bypasses `scrub()` — no bulk action, no callback, no manual dial.
- Caller IDs live in their own table so a number can be retired without losing its history.
- Recording filenames use the last four digits of the phone, not the full number.
- Depth over coverage on compliance work — a thin version is worse than none, because I would trust something that hadn't earned it.
- Every prompt to Claude Code must end with an instruction to test and verify in the real browser and reconcile on-screen numbers against the database.

